<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 181 0 R
/E (Supported wet lab development of a mechanical stretch assay to study platlet-rich-plasma \(PRP\) effects on tendon progenitor cells \(TPCs\) from chronic tendinopathy patients. The assay modeled tendon loading in vitro and contributed to a larger effort to standardize PRP and develop IRB-ready clinical protocols.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 181 0 R
/E (Chronic tendinopathy remains difficult to treat due to poor healing and limited regenerative options. While PRP is a promising biologic therapy, clinical outcomes are inconsistent due to variability in preparation and a lack of standardized testing platforms. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
